<title>USA: Litchfield arranges credit lines.</title>
<headline>Litchfield arranges credit lines.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Vt. 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Litchfield Financial Corp said it has increased its revolving credit facility with BankBoston/Fleet Bank to $50 million from $30 million.</p>
<p>The company's total total credit facilities rose to $106 million after this deal, which included a three year commitment, Litchfield said in a statement.</p>
<p>Also, Litchfield said it has placed $15.3 million in loans to rural land dealers and resort developers secured by consumer receivables with a bank in its first securitization of those type of loans.</p>
</text>
